First, I'd like to comment that, while this topic isn't directly related
to NH, some of the ideas could be implemented in future versions, and
besides, I think that many of the NH players would be interested in the
discussion anyways.  If not, tell us to move to a different group.  At
the very least, it's more interesting reading than some of the technical
installation questions on the group (a necessary evil).

I don't like I.C.E.'s Rolemaster because of the sheer complexity (and
enormous size) of the weapons tables.  A 20 by ~100 array for each weapon?
I DO like the detail in the critical hits table...  The armor seems
to be sort of limiting, though.  'Only 20 types' doesn't allow for much
in the way of "You find a pair of gauntlets of power."

I'd prefer to see a combat system based on GURPS, with separate armor
for each part of the body and intelligent monsters being able to strike
at the more unprotected regions...  Also, chances for dodging, blocking
(shield), and parrying attacks.

The perviously suggested features of "real-light" areas and wandering,
belligerent monsters (who kill other monsters) don't interest me as much
as a realistic combat system does.  Start with a good combat system (which
is what most of these games are about, even NH3.0 :-) ), and the rest of
the game follows from that.

Oh, and BTW, I _would_ like to see my numbers on the screen to accurately
judge how well I'm doing.

